From 4772dc7c8b69e545be5fa131e0a008b81da4c4ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duck-brain <duck-brain@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:14:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] duck-brain P13: the tick journal (`robotd --journal
 <file>`)

One JSON line per control tick, for replaying a run through the same
network on a PC and comparing bit for bit (duck-brain
scripts/replay_journal.py):

- header: robotd version, rate, joint names and ids, [bus], [feetech],
  [body_imu] and [policy] as loaded;
- per tick: time, the label, the network that drove (slot, file, the
  exact input row fed to it, its action, the scale multiplier and its
  targets), the targets handed to safety, the gain, the positions,
  velocities and IMU sample read, and the bus's own view
  (RobotIo::journal; on the Feetech bus: position and voltage registers
  per servo with null for a missed answer, goal registers sent,
  smoothed V and the error factor, read time, observation age, IMU
  sample number and age);
- an end line with lines written and dropped.

Floats are written as the shortest decimal of their f64 value, an f32
widened exactly first, so narrowing a value read back gives the bits the
policy saw. Lines go through a bounded queue to a writer thread: the
control thread never waits on the disk, and a full queue drops and
counts.
